 <div class="analytics-query-stats"><p><strong><?=A::number((int)$searchConsole['clicks'])?></strong><span>Clicks in imported rows</span></p><p><strong><?=A::number((int)$searchConsole['impressions'])?></strong><span>Impressions in imported rows</span></p><p><strong><?=$searchConsole['ctr']===null?'—':number_format((float)$searchConsole['ctr'],2).'%'?></strong><span>Click-through rate</span></p></div>
 <div class="analytics-grid"><div><h3>Leading queries by clicks</h3><?php A::bars(array_slice($searchConsole['rows'],0,8),'query','clicks','No query clicks in this snapshot.',(int)$searchConsole['clicks']); ?></div><div><p class="small muted">Google omits some queries to protect privacy and may export only its top rows. Imported-row totals can therefore be lower than the totals shown in Search Console. A query cannot be connected to a particular visitor in this dashboard.</p><p class="small"><a class="text-link" href="https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/7576553?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">About Search Console reporting ↗</a></p></div></div>
 <details class="analytics-detail"><summary>View query details (up to 100 leading rows)</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table class="content-table"><caption class="sr-only">Imported Google Search Console query performance</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Query</th><th scope="col">Clicks</th><th scope="col">Impressions</th><th scope="col">CTR</th><th scope="col">Average position</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach ($searchConsole['rows'] as $query): ?><tr><td><?=e($query['query'])?></td><td><?=A::number((int)$query['clicks'])?></td><td><?=A::number((int)$query['impressions'])?></td><td><?=number_format((float)$query['ctr'],2)?>%</td><td><?=number_format((float)$query['position'],1)?></td></tr><?php endforeach; ?></tbody></table></div></details>
 <?php else: ?><p class="analytics-empty">No Search Console report has been imported. Your visitor analytics can still identify Google referrals when a referrer is supplied.</p><?php endif; ?>
 <details class="analytics-detail"><summary><?=$searchConsole['query_count']?'Replace the imported query report':'Import a query report'?></summary><p>In Search Console, choose your website, open <strong>Performance → Search results</strong>, select a date range, and export the <strong>Queries</strong> table as CSV. Use the English column headings. Import the same dates below. Importing replaces the previous query snapshot after the whole file has passed validation.</p><form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="form-stack"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="query-import"><label for="analytics-query-file">Queries CSV<input id="analytics-query-file" type="file" name="queries" accept=".csv,text/csv" required></label><div class="analytics-query-dates"><label for="query-start">Export period starts<input id="query-start" name="query_start" type="date" max="<?=gmdate('Y-m-d')?>" required></label><label for="query-end">Export period ends<input id="query-end" name="query_end" type="date" max="<?=gmdate('Y-m-d')?>" required></label></div><p class="small muted">Up to 2 MiB and 5,000 query rows. Expected columns: Top queries, Clicks, Impressions, CTR, Position. No Google password or access token is needed for a CSV import.</p><button class="button" type="submit">Import query report</button></form></details>
 <?php if ($searchConsole['query_count']): ?><details class="analytics-detail"><summary>Remove this imported snapshot</summary><p>Remove the imported query rows. You can import the original CSV again later.</p><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="query-clear"><button class="button secondary" type="submit">Remove imported query report</button></form></details><?php endif; ?>
